// A pull-rod holds an ore hopper's gate open. A rod stands up beside a hopper's bin and runs along the floor to a tread
// plate. The hopper holds four stones and has no cart under it, so its gate is shut. The mole steps onto the plate: the
// rod is pulled and holds the gate open, and the stones come down onto the floor. It steps off: the gate shuts again.
map
####################################
#..................................#
#..................................#
#..................................#
#.......................F..........#
#.......................F..........#
#.......................F..........#
#.......................F..........#
#.......................F..........#
#.......................F..........#
#.......................F......@...#
########################FFFFee######
####################################
end
give OreHopper 1
place 2 -11 -1 OreHopper
expect 3 bins == 1
drop 5 Stone -11 -8
drop 10 Stone -11 -8
drop 15 Stone -11 -8
drop 20 Stone -11 -8
expect 60 binload == 4                // held, gate shut
expect 60 binopen == 0
hold 70-74 left                       // onto the plate
expect 100 binopen == 1               // the rod holds it open...
expect 140 binload == 0               // ...and it empties
expect 140 zone:Stone,-12,-10,-2,0 == 4   // onto the floor under its spout
hold 150-160 right                    // off the plate
expect 180 binopen == 0
